# Architecture Review Knowledge - Cursor Rules

## Current Product Context

This repository manages the lifecycle of reusable Architecture Review Knowledge.
The Failure Model is one curated knowledge product.

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/traceability/registry.md` before making structural or
knowledge-lifecycle changes.

## Trust Zones

- `knowledge/raw-notes/`: unverified; Production use prohibited.
- `knowledge/candidates/`: provisional; Production use prohibited.
- `knowledge/curated/`: approved knowledge products.
- `knowledge/sources/`: public-safe evidence metadata and anchors.

Follow `policies/retrieval-policy.md`,
`policies/promotion-policy.md`, and
`policies/information-handling-policy.md`.

## Failure Model

- Success Criteria (`sc-*`):
  `knowledge/curated/failure-model/success-criteria/`
- Symptoms (`rf-*`):
  `knowledge/curated/failure-model/symptoms/`
- Root Causes (`rc-*`):
  `knowledge/curated/failure-model/root-causes/`

Canonical schema: `schemas/failure-model/node-spec.md`.

Relationship vocabulary:

- `triggers` / `triggered_by`
- `threatens` / `threatened_by`
- `leads_to` / `leads_from`

Do not use superseded relationship names such as `caused_by`,
`triggers_symptoms`, `triggers_root_causes`, or `explained_by`.

## Tooling

`tooling/miro-to-failure-model/` is the active Miro conversion adapter.
Its Gherkin contracts are under `tooling/miro-to-failure-model/docs/specs/`.

MCP and RAG are not part of the current product baseline.

## Language

Repository-facing durable assets are written in English. Chat may use Japanese.
